# tinval.ref  --  reference / contract data for test/init/tinval.f
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose: documents the expected behaviour of modern/init/initval.f,
#          the bitwise initialisation-state validator.
#
# Contract under test (assumed cross-agent interface):
#   SUBROUTINE INITVAL ( NDIV )
#     INTEGER NDIV   ! out: count of bitwise divergences of the modern
#                    !      init state vs the legacy BLOCK DATA values;
#                    !      0 == perfect bitwise match.
#   Guard clause: 'IF (IDIAG .EQ. 0) RETURN' is the first executable
#   statement, so INITVAL runs only when diagnostics are enabled by
#   modern/diag/diagctl.f from NASTRAN_INIT_VALIDATE=1.
#
# Format:  comment lines begin with '#'; data lines are 'KEY VALUE'.
# Run with NASTRAN_INIT_VALIDATE=1 and NASTRAN_LEGACY_INIT unset.
# EXPECT_VERDICT PASS: TINVAL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Binding assertions consumed by tinval.f:
#   EXPDIV = 0 -> zero divergences after a correct modern init.
#   EXPRAN = 1 -> the validator must actually execute (NDIV set away
#                 from the driver's 999999 sentinel), proving the
#                 NASTRAN_INIT_VALIDATE gate is honoured. tinval.f also
#                 calls INITVAL twice and requires an identical result
#                 (the validator must be side-effect-free / idempotent).
EXPDIV 0
EXPRAN 1
# end of tinval.ref
